LYATH'S DEFENDER BUFF — SPXDEFBUFF, NOT SHIPPED: no gain. Against main 03b661d (v6.21).
New judge reader `abDefenderBuff(g, seat, uid)` -> {cost} when an ability's parsed ops carry a defender buff
(DEFENDER_BUFF_OPS = ["defActBuff"]); pool census: exactly one ability, Lyath's hero power ("The crowd boos
you. Defending action cards you control get +1{d} this turn." -> [defActBuff 1, boo 1]; the boo makes a Might).
Policy (gate SPXDEFBUFF, keys rxDefBuff / holdDefBuff): own turn, hold it unless floating resources already pay
for it; defending, activate it when the wall holds hand cards and the hit still leaks.
Lyath own seat, rule policy, 28 games/seed, 3 seeds paired:
  hold + defend:               7.67 -> 5.00 (-2.67, t -4.00)   8→4 7→5 8→6
  defend only (no hold; env SPXDEFBUFF_NOHOLD=1): 7.67 -> 6.67 (-1.00, t -1.00)   8→5 7→7 8→8
The own-turn use is NOT wasted: its rider (a Might token, +1{p} to the next attack every turn) is worth the
{r}{r}, and paying {r}{r} on the opponent's turn costs pitched cards for +1{d} a blocker. Parked.
Apply: git apply experiments/spxdefbuff.patch

